---
description: Use Context7 for library APIs, pinned to this repo's installed versions
alwaysApply: true
---

When using an external library API (Vitest, Testing Library, React, Vite, Next, MUI, etc.):

1. Read this project's dependency files first (`package.json`, lockfile). Use the **installed** version, not the latest on the internet.
2. Call Context7 MCP only: `resolve-library-id`, then `query-docs`. Do not web-search for Context7 or as a substitute when MCP is connected.
3. Prefer a **versioned** Context7 library ID (`/org/project/version`) that matches our installed version (same major; closest listed version if an exact match is missing).
4. Do not upgrade packages, change `package.json`, or switch APIs (for example Vitest Browser Mode vs jsdom) unless the user asked for an upgrade.
5. If Context7 docs and this repo disagree, follow this repo.

Do not invent method names from memory.
